# ============================================================================
# NOTES
# ============================================================================
#
# Rationale for parameter reduction:
#
# 1. Sensitivity analysis showed that 99.9% of flux variance is explained by
#    the 3 photosynthesis parameters (slatop, leafcn, flnr)
#
# 2. All 17 root parameters combined account for <0.1% of variance
#
# 3. With only 3 annual observations (GPP, ER, NEE), we cannot reliably
#    constrain 20 parameters - this leads to non-identifiability
#
# 4. The initial 20-parameter MCMC had:
#    - ESS = 6-7 (need >100)
#    - Acceptance rate = 6.3% (target 20-40%)
#    - Perfect parameter correlations (r > 0.99)
#    - Condition number = 2.86×10⁷ (severely ill-conditioned)
#
# 5. By fixing insensitive parameters at reasonable values, we achieve:
#    - Identifiable parameter estimates
#    - Proper MCMC convergence
#    - Meaningful uncertainty quantification
#    - Computational efficiency (faster mixing)
#
# Expected MCMC performance with this file:
# - Acceptance rate: 20-40% (optimal range)
# - ESS: >1000 (good mixing)
# - Autocorrelation time: <100 iterations
# - Parameter correlations: <0.7 (manageable)
#
# The root parameters are fixed at their best estimates from the initial
# wide-range MCMC, which are physiologically reasonable and consistent with
# Wang et al. (2023) reported values for temperate deciduous forests.
